course: dictionary
lesson: 4060
title: The word genius
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A genius is a person who is extremely clever or talented. Read the context: «Theo decided he was a tech genius and turned the router off and on forty times in one evening.» Turning a router on and off forty times is not a clever plan, so Theo is joking about himself. The context shows that genius is being used with a bit of humour.
explain: Genius can also mean very great cleverness or skill, the talent itself. Here it has no "a" in front of it, because it names a quality, not a person. Test it by swapping in your meaning: "She showed great skill" fits, so the meaning is right.
explain: In casual talk, «That's genius!» means that is a clever idea. Context helps again: people say it about a neat trick, not about a person. But teachers warn that calling a child «you're a genius» is empty praise. Better praise says what the child did, like "tell me about it".
fact: A genius is a person who is extremely clever or talented. The plural is geniuses.
fact: Genius without "a" means very great cleverness or skill, the talent itself.
fact: «A stroke of genius» means one very clever idea.
fact: «A genius at» something means very skilled at that thing, such as «a genius at chess».
fact: Informal: «That's genius!» means that is a clever idea, said about a trick or plan.
exercise: «Theo decided he was a tech genius and turned the router off and on forty times in one evening.» What does genius mean here? | *Someone extremely clever or talented with tech | A router that is broken | Someone who is very tired | A kind of game
exercise: Jade says «That's genius!» about a trick. What does she mean? | That is a very long idea | *That is a clever idea | That is an idea that failed | That is a rude idea
exercise: Teachers say praising effort, with "tell me about it", helps more than «you're a genius». Why? | Because it means nothing at all | *Because it says what the child did and invites them to talk about it | Because it makes children cleverer by magic | Because genius is a bad word
test: What is the plural of genius? | *Geniuses | Genius | Genuses | Genies
test: «A stroke of genius» means? | A quick push | *A very clever idea | A stroke on the head | A slow walk home
exam: Does a big game need one genius? | Yes, only maths geniuses can work on games | Yes, one genius in a bedroom makes it all | *No, over 300 people, from programmers to testers, can make one together | No, games are never made by anyone
